{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqq0q02xylw","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Drop production cosine autowire floor 0.55 to 0; eager-judge arbitrates; bounded by FANOUT not floor","summary":"DECISION (2026-06-22, user-directed): production SEMANTIC_AUTOWIRE_THRESHOLD default drops from 0.55 to 0 (daemon.js:1675) so autowire seeds the top-per-kind candidates unconditionally and the eager-judge arbitrates keep/prune — cosine is no longer a floor, only a ranking signal. Env override (ORCH_AUTOWIRE_THRESHOLD) stays intact. CONSEQUENCES (intended, not bugs): (1) every new node now seeds up to TASK_CREATE_FANOUT=5 notes + 5 tasks and triggers an eager-judge pass — previously ONLY nodes with a >=0.55 neighbor did. Per-node judge cost stays bounded by FANOUT (<=10 candidates, one judge call), but judging now runs on EVERY new node, so judge spend rises on active workspaces. (2) every new node now passes the JUDGING->READY claim gate (routes/overlay.js:466) until judged or timed-out, so eager-judge LATENCY is now in the task-claimable critical path. That coupling is why a fast SYNCHRONOUS in-process judge (P1: sync judge-drain reusing buildJudgePrompt + runJudgeLoop from lib/headless-drain.js) lands together with the floor drop, not after. TRADEOFF accepted: replace a free but brittle cosine cutoff with a paid LLM judge that recovers real context edges the 0.55 floor was silently dropping. Shipped as feature orch/feature/bench-prod-parity (P1 sync judge, P2 drop floor). Enables bench parity: once prod default is 0/uncapped, the bench drops its ORCH_AUTOWIRE_THRESHOLD=0.0 / K=20 overrides and runs prod defaults with zero divergence.","category":null,"tags":["autowire","eager-judge","daemon","parity","feature:bench-prod-parity"],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-23T02:21:24.585Z","vec":[-0.09315681457519531,-0.010917727835476398,0.005109439138323069,0.031947437673807144,0.0764017328619957,-0.06318426877260208,-0.01862742379307747,0.02886364981532097,-0.00524182710796